codex
A full Base-universe inspection found one additional representable frozen case that the numeric-only inventory missed: `SortVal` does contain `SortStr`, so string concatenation is in scope. I’m adding the exact `seqConcat` recurrence and covering both canonical and nested iterable string encodings; list concatenation is not an `applyBin` rule in this semantics—it is a higher-priority allocating `<k>` rule—so it must not be fabricated in this pure dispatcher.
apply patch
